---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of use · Gadgets Bidding"
  description="Gadgets Bidding terms for bidding, payments, seller fees, delivery, refunds, and disputes."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <p class="meta">Effective 1 September 2026</p>
  <h1>Terms of use</h1>
  <article>
    <section>
      <h2>Eligibility</h2>
      <p>
        Gadgets Bidding is for people aged 18 and over in Nigeria. You must
        provide accurate account details and keep your login secure.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Bid commitment</h2>
      <p>
        You need at least ₦1,000 available in your wallet to place a bid.
        When you are the current winning bidder, this amount is held as a
        commitment deposit. It is released if you are outbid or when you
        complete payment.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Winning bid payment</h2>
      <p>
        If you win an auction, pay within 24 hours. If payment is missed,
        the ₦1,000 commitment is forfeited, your account is suspended, and
        reactivation requires a ₦5,000 penalty.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Second-place buyer</h2>
      <p>
        If the winning bidder misses payment, Gadgets Bidding may offer the item
        to the next eligible bidder at their last bid amount.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2 id="seller-fees">Seller fees</h2>
      <p>
        Sellers are charged a 5% platform fee on successful sales. The app
        shows estimated payout before a seller lists an auction.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Backoffice delivery</h2>
      <p>
        Sellers send sold items to Gadgets Bidding backoffice first. Backoffice
        confirms receipt, handles buyer delivery, and updates tracking
        where available.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2 id="disputes">Refunds and disputes</h2>
      <p>
        Refunds and payout holds are reviewed by backoffice. Opening a
        dispute can hold seller payout until the issue is resolved.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms:
        <a href="mailto:support@gadgetsbidding.com">support@gadgetsbidding.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>

</Legal>
